s\\n\\nFEED https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\\n- US crypto ATM operator Bitcoin Depot files for Chapter 11 to wind down business - The Block\\n- Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Fall Amid Trump's 'Clock Is Ticking' Iran Warning: Analyst Says BTC Can Slip If This 'Important' Support Is Lost - Yahoo Finance\\n- Verus-Ethereum bridge loses $11 million as hackers keep targeting cross-chain infrastructure - CoinDesk\\n- Crypto crash: why are Bitcoin Cash, LUNC, Pi Network, WLFI going down? - TradingView\\n- Bitcoin (BTC) Hits Two-Week Low as Crypto Liquidations Top Half a Billion - Bloomberg.com\"}],\"details\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"exitCode\":0,\"durationMs\":1304,\"aggregated\":\"FEED https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\\n- Crypto security is turning into an AI arms race as agents may overwhelm compliance teams\\n- Aave restores ether borrowing limits after $230 million exploit\\n- Bitcoin Depot, North America's largest bitcoin ATM operator, files for bankruptcy\\n- Iran may be turning the Strait of Hormuz into a bitcoin-based insurance market, local reports say\\n- Crypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most\\n\\nFEED https://cointelegraph.com/rss\\n- Surging oil prices have been driving Ether selling pressure: Tom Lee\\n- Reports suggest Iran is mulling Hormuz ‘insurance’ scheme, paid in Bitcoin\\n- Senate crypto bill at risk beyond midterms if not passed by August: NYDIG\\n- Analysts debate whether Bitcoin is in ‘sell in May’ bear market setup\\n- WETH markets return to normal operations on Aave amid rsETH recovery progress\\n\\nFEED https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\\n- US crypto ATM operator Bitcoin Depot files for Chapter 11 to wind down business - The Block\\n- Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Fall Amid Trump's 'Clock Is Ticking' Iran Warning: Analyst Says BTC Can Slip If This 'Important' Support Is Lost - Yahoo Finance\\n- Verus-Ethereum bridge loses $11 million as hackers keep targeting cross-chain infrastructure - CoinDesk\\n- Crypto crash: why are Bitcoin Cash, LUNC, Pi Network, WLFI going down? - TradingView\\n- Bitcoin (BTC) Hits Two-Week Low as Crypto Liquidations Top Half a Billion - Bloomberg.com\",\"cwd\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779091605665},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I found one clear shared story for today — the Iran/Hormuz bitcoin-insurance angle. I’m checking it for duplicates and pulling the source text now.\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_tBkByiLOkdrY5uzULIQkEI7Q\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"bash ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/history/article_history.sh check \\\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/iran-may-be-turning-the-strait-of-hormuz-into-a-bitcoin-insurance-market-local-reports-say\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\",\"timeout\":30}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_rjREUNUAWLBEVmhpkFJAWypx\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"curl -o /dev/null -s -w \\\"%{http_code}\\\\n\\\" \\\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/iran-may-be-turning-the-strait-of-hormuz-into-a-bitcoin-insurance-market-local-reports-say\\\" && curl -o /dev/null -s -w \\\"%{http_code}\\\\n\\\" \\\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/iran-mulls-platform-for-ships-transiting-strait-of-hormuz-to-pay-in-bitcoin-report?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\",\"timeout\":60}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_SLO3rdOAgtamZOmrz33NkS91\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"trafilatura -u \\\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/iran-may-be-turning-the-strait-of-hormuz-into-a-bitcoin-insurance-market-local-reports-say\\\" --output-format markdown | head -c 12000\",\"workdir\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\",\"timeout\":60}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_qltv24PO1Qc6uhBAVpwwStez\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"trafilatura -u \\\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/iran-mulls-platform-for-ships-transiting-strait-of-hormuz-to-pay-in-bitcoin-report?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\\\" --output-format markdown | head -c 12000\",\"workdir\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\",\"timeout\":60}}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4-mini\",\"usage\":{\"input\":5847,\"output\":733,\"cacheRead\":12928,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":19508,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1779091605666,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-DgnHtU2FiAFlGQzmmcx6a4TNRMsz6\"},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_tBkByiLOkdrY5uzULIQkEI7Q\",\"toolName\":\"exec\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"NOT_FOUND\"}],\"details\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"exitCode\":0,\"durationMs\":33,\"aggregated\":\"NOT_FOUND\",\"cwd\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779091614389},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_rjREUNUAWLBEVmhpkFJAWypx\",\"toolName\":\"exec\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"429\\n200\"}],\"details\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"exitCode\":0,\"durationMs\":2887,\"aggregated\":\"429\\n200\",\"cwd\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779091614389},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_SLO3rdOAgtamZOmrz33NkS91\",\"toolName\":\"exec\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"(no output)\"}],\"details\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"exitCode\":0,\"durationMs\":975,\"aggregated\":\"\",\"cwd\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779091614389},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_qltv24PO1Qc6uhBAVpwwStez\",\"toolName\":\"exec\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Control over the Strait of Hormuz has been the leading issue in the US-Iran war. The shipping lane handles about one-fifth of the global oil trade. Many ships have been prevented from transiting the strait after the US started launching airstrikes in Iran in late February.\\n\\nMedia reports state that Iran collected its first revenue from tolls imposed on ships transiting the Strait last month. Prior to the US-Iran war, no such measures were in place.\\n\\nFars News said the insurance platform seeks to distinguish between transit vessels from different countries.\\n\\n“Under the Economy Ministry's plan, managing the Strait through an insurance framework would enable the issuance of various marine insurance policies as well as certificates of financial responsibility,” Fars News said, adding it could generate over $10 billion in revenue for the country.\\n\\nThere is no guarantee that Iran will go ahead with the insurance proposal, and the website purporting to offer “Iranian Digital Insurance” could be fake. The website was down at the time of writing.\\n\\nScammers have previously defrauded shipping companies operating in the Strait of Hormuz by demanding payment in cryptocurrency for safe passage.\\n\\nDescription of Hormuz Safe seeking to accept shipper tolls in Bitcoin. Source: Google\\n\\nDemanding insurance payments in Bitcoin could make sense, given that US authorities froze $344 million worth of USDT tied to Iran last month.\\n\\nEarlier reports said Iran had been accepting oil tolls in US dollar-denominated stablecoins such as Tether USDt (USDT), as well as Bitcoin and fiat currencies such as the Chinese yuan, with USDT reportedly the preferred cryptocurrency.\\n\\n**Related: ****UAE investors buy AI dip, keep crypto exposure despite conflict**** **\\n\\nIndustry leaders have touted Bitcoin as a more appropriate cryptocurrency for sanctioned countries because it is sufficiently decentralized and has no issuer capable of freezing funds.\\n\\nIn early April, a spokesperson for Iran’s Oil, Gas and Petrochemical Products Exporters’ Union said certain ships would be able to pass through the strait provided that they pay a tariff of $1 per barrel of oil in Bitcoin.\\n\\n“Once the email arrives and Iran completes its assessment, vessels are given a few seconds to pay in Bitcoin, ensuring they can’t be traced or confiscated due to sanctions,” they said at the time.\\n\\n**Magazine: ****Adam Back says current demand is ‘almost’ enough to send Bitcoin to $1M**\\n\\nMore on the subject\"}],\"details\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"exitCode\":0,\"durationMs\":2941,\"aggregated\":\"Control over the Strait of Hormuz has been the leading issue in the US-Iran war. The shipping lane handles about one-fifth of the global oil trade. Many ships have been prevented from transiting the strait after the US started launching airstrikes in Iran in late February.\\n\\nMedia reports state that Iran collected its first revenue from tolls imposed on ships transiting the Strait last month. Prior to the US-Iran war, no such measures were in place.\\n\\nFars News said the insurance platform seeks to distinguish between transit vessels from different countries.\\n\\n“Under the Economy Ministry's plan, managing the Strait through an insurance framework would enable the issuance of various marine insurance policies as well as certificates of financial responsibility,” Fars News said, adding it could generate over $10 billion in revenue for the country.\\n\\nThere is no guarantee that Iran will go ahead with the insurance proposal, and the website purporting to offer “Iranian Digital Insurance” could be fake. The website was down at the time of writing.\\n\\nScammers have previously defrauded shipping companies operating in the Strait of Hormuz by demanding payment in cryptocurrency for safe passage.\\n\\nDescription of Hormuz Safe seeking to accept shipper tolls in Bitcoin. Source: Google\\n\\nDemanding insurance payments in Bitcoin could make sense, given that US authorities froze $344 million worth of USDT tied to Iran last month.\\n\\nEarlier reports said Iran had been accepting oil tolls in US dollar-denominated stablecoins such as Tether USDt (USDT), as well as Bitcoin and fiat currencies such as the Chinese yuan, with USDT reportedly the preferred cryptocurrency.\\n\\n**Related: ****UAE investors buy AI dip, keep crypto exposure despite conflict**** **\\n\\nIndustry leaders have touted Bitcoin as a more appropriate cryptocurrency for sanctioned countries because it is sufficiently decentralized and has no issuer capable of freezing funds.\\n\\nIn early April, a spokesperson for Iran’s Oil, Gas and Petrochemical Products Exporters’ Union said certain ships would be able to pass through the strait provided that they pay a tariff of $1 per barrel of oil in Bitcoin.\\n\\n“Once the email arrives and Iran completes its assessment, vessels are given a few seconds to pay in Bitcoin, ensuring they can’t be traced or confiscated due to sanctions,” they said at the time.\\n\\n**Magazine: ****Adam Back says current demand is ‘almost’ enough to send Bitcoin to $1M**\\n\\nMore on the subject\",\"cwd\":\"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1779091614389},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The CoinDesk page is throttling direct extraction, so I’m trying a clean fallback to recover the article text without guessing.\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_rwNTbgFH5m5pC9M6QfBE27pC\",\"name\":\"exec\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport requests\\nurl='https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/iran-may-be-turning-the-strait-of-hormuz-into-a-bitcoin-insurance-market-local-reports-say'\\nheaders={'User-Agent':'Mozilla/5.0'}\\nr=requests.get(url,headers=headers,timeout=20)\\nprint(r.status_code)\\nprint(r.text[:5000])\\nPY\",\"workdir\":\"/home/bhard/.ope